A||||6||Shaun41178||Raced a 3rd Gen GTA||||14||
Z||000000||Shaun41178||10-21-2000||03:44 AM||||Yep people, doing the weekend tradition.  This time I was challenged!!  Never happens but cool when it does.<P>White Firebird GTA pulls alongside and starts jumping it.  I assume it is a 350 cause it is an auto and I think GTA's came with 350's.  So I goose it a couple of times to let him know I am game.  His exhaust sounded like it had a hole in it somewhere around the muffler.  Not a bad sound but like not a good throaty clear rumble to it.<P>First off someone needs to teach this guy how to race.  He pulls up alongside of me and gooses the throttle and is waiting for me to jump it so he can nail it.  Thing is is that there was a car ahead of me but not him.  He would not speed up so we could get around the car.  Its like he wanted me to race him but have to slow down for the car ahead so he could stay in it and beat me if he wanted.  Well finally after about a mile he passes the car so I sling around side of him and get even with him doing about 45.  He is goosing it so I do it just enough to get him to lay into to it all the way.  That is when I lay into it hard and start walking this guy.  Not much but I was slowly pulling on him.  More at the slower speeds then top end.  We go a few times and each time I walk about a car from 45-85 or so.  We catch a light and we are both in the front.  He has his window down and says he just installed a fresh 350 a few weeks back and didn't want to get on it too hard.  I was like yea right pal you were hard on it the whole time we were running.  I could hear his engine over mine running up to redline!!  Anyways I asked him if he had a bigger cam in it and he said yea.  He said like 2 steps up from a stock cam.  I am guessing he had other stuff done to it as well if he had a cam in it too.  Bolt on stuff anyways.<P>I think he was embarrased that he got beat by  a Fiero which is why he said he didn't get on it hard.  At least that is my belief.<P>We didn't go when the light we were at turned green cause he was still talking to me when it turned green and I didn't want to be disrespectfull by peeling out while he was talking.  I just let him drive off and wonder. <P>Another kill for the "Small Red Machine"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||14
Z||000001||batboy||10-21-2000||08:19 AM||||The GTA's are supposed to have 350 engines, but when I was looking to buy a GTA a couple years ago before I bought the Batmobile, my experience was that most of the ones with GTA emblems on them are fakes (counterfeit). They usually were a dressed up Trans Am's with a 305 motor. The front side fender vents are a dead giveaway. The GTA don't have them, but the regular TA's do. The GTA's also have the wrap around rear spoiler, but many of the fake ones have that too. There is a way to code them off the VIN too, plus a real GTA with have the proper option group listed on the plate located inside the console.||||reg||1
